{"Device limit cache bypass: AnonDeviceService.tagDeviceUI caches the device ID before persisting it, and Anonymous.Authenticate now blocks only on ErrDeviceLimitReached; after the first rejection, subsequent requests for that same device skip persistence due to the cache and anonymous auth succeeds. This breaks the new device-limit enforcement for at least the local cache TTL (29 minutes). The fix is to move a.localCache.SetDefault(key, struct{}{}) to after successful CreateOrUpdateDevice, or keep an in-flight marker but delete the key on error.": 0.8802916407585144}